title: mf hash
tags: [[CLI command]] [[File fingerprint]]
kind: reference
summary: Compute the content hashes of the files a query selects

Starts a hash task and follows it to the end, printing how many files were hashed,
reused or skipped. Every ''file'' the query selects gets its partial and full hash
with the `stat` stamp they were taken under; a directory or a symlink has none, and
a file under an offline volume is left frozen. A stored hash whose stamp still
matches the file is reused, unless `--rehash`; a file that changed while it was read
is skipped rather than given a hash of no state it was in.

```
mf hash 'mfr_path ->* "/photos"'
mf hash -s 'mfr_type=file' --rehash
```

Files marked with <<cmd "mf_hash">> keep their hash fresh on their own; this
computes hashes for any set, at once ([[Content hashes kept fresh]]). The hashes are
the ones the duplicate scan reuses ([[The duplicate hash cache]]).
